##
## Filters for tests that fail only in ASAN/LSAN builds on Linux
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue.
##

# Upstream Chromium test. Brave patches ResetReportUploader::
# DispatchReportInternal() to return early (the feature is disabled), so the
# uploader that this test allocates with `new` never deletes itself and
# LeakSanitizer reports it. ASAN/LSAN-only: other builds do not check for
# leaks. Brave's own ResetReportUploaderTest.NoFetch covers this code without
# leaking. Stable upstream: 0.0% flake rate over 30 days per LUCI Analysis
# (check-upstream-flake.py), so this is Brave-specific.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/59254
-ResetReportUploaderTest.NoCrash
